  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "Democratic lawmakers, led by Sen. Ed Markey, are questioning the constitutionality of a U.S. Border Patrol predictive intelligence program that uses license plate readers to flag and detain drivers based on travel patterns. The scrutiny follows an AP investigation revealing the nationwide program, which also taps data from other federal, state, local, and private LPR sources.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Such pervasive surveillance \u2014 similar to surveillance conducted by authoritarian regimes such as China \u2014 not only chills lawful expression and assembly but also raises serious constitutional concerns.",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    },
    {
      "quote": "A network of cameras scans and records vehicle license plate information, and an algorithm flags vehicles deemed suspicious based on where they came from, where they were going and which route they took.",
      "paragraph_idx": 20
    }
  ],
